{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/710139-the-language-of-hobgoblins","id":710139,"title":"The Language of Hobgoblins","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-10-20T01:26:55-07:00","id":710139,"title":"The Language of Hobgoblins","content":"What language do hobgoblins speak? If so, do they each have different languages? Do they speak their own language? A version of D&amp;D's Supernal (they understand everybody, everybody understands them)? Do they mostly speak the languages of the local humans? I am not entirely sure which I prefer. At times language confusion can be fun, but at the same time, I don't want players to dismiss talking out of hand, nor do I want to have them spend more merits on languages than they already have (living in Miami all actually spend xp on speaking English and Spanish, a few also took French and Russian because of background reasons).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4560-madfox11","name":"Madfox11","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-20T03:13:34-07:00","id":710279,"title":"","content":"I would think that they mostly speak local human languages, or are at least fluent in them. After all, many hobgoblins engage in trade with humans and changelings, which is difficult without a common language. Also, I believe that some hobgoblins were once human, though I'm not sure of the reference. Certainly Hedge Beasts may once have been mundane animals, at which point they may have picked up some understanding of human speech.<br /> <br /> That's not to say that they sound exactly like humans in the area. There may be hedge-specific dialects, particular breeds of hobgoblin may be physically unable to pronounce words in the same way as human speakers, and time distortion in the Hedge may mean that archaic speech, dead languages, or even slang from the future is mixed into the general patois.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Not the <a href=\"https://www.theoi.com/Daimon/Alastor.html\" target=\"_blank\">daimon</a>, just a namesake.","edited":{"userid":858,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/858-alastor","user":"Alastor","date":". 10-20-2015, 06:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/858-alastor","name":"Alastor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-20T03:20:20-07:00","id":710282,"title":"","content":"They can probably buy fluency in whatever language they need at the markets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-20T11:06:58-07:00","id":710960,"title":"","content":"You could say that hobgoblins with the capacity and inclination to speak mortal languages develop the &quot;Wisdom Of Dreams&quot; Merit (Rites Of Spring, page 97), or a Fae Aspect that imitates it. That way, they can wake up each day knowing one language well enough to get most ideas and messages across, in addition to the languages they learned normally. Complex communication might require an Exceptional Success. What Alastor said is also very true, and it contributes to the atmosphere of weirdness and byzantine customs of goblin markets.<br /> <br /> That being said, a goblin merchant trying to explain financial speculation among its kimd would make little to no sense to most clients, even if he had no accent at all. Their minds tend to be strange like that. Besides, nothing prevents a goblin merchant from using drawings, gestures and gibberish with the right tone to explain their wares and prices. A miscommunication in this case is all too easy, and poor communication in deals with goblins is not a bright idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 10-20-2015, 04:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-20T13:00:55-07:00","id":711140,"title":"","content":"I'd say they speak Babbelfish, which mean their speech automatically translates into whatever language the listener is most fluent in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-20T22:44:33-07:00","id":711847,"title":"","content":"Depends on the individual hobgoblin, I'd wager.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4968-mrbreaksit","name":"MrBreaksIt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}